.TH DANBY 1
.SH NAME
danby \- collection of ODE-based physical, biological, and economic models for Wm
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/
.I name
.br
.B wmapp /Apps/!Danby
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B danby
programs are interactive numerical-integration demonstrations in the spirit of
James Danby's
.I Computer Modeling: From Sports to Spaceflight, From Order to Chaos
and companion texts: each poses an ordinary-differential-equation model,
integrates it live with
.IR numerics (2)'s
fourth-order Runge-Kutta stepper (or, for the adaptive-step lessons, an
embedded RKF4(5) pair), and redraws its state as parameters or initial
conditions change under the pointer or a set of parameter tracks.
.PP
Each program may be started as
.BI danby/ name
or from the
.B !Danby
pinboard folder; the related
.B !Models
and
.B !Lessons
folders group the same programs by subject and by teaching sequence.
Unless its own page says otherwise, each program pauses and resumes with
.BR space ,
steps one displayed increment with
.B period
while paused, restarts from its default state with
.BR r ,
and quits with
.B q
or
.BR Escape .
.PP
A handful of the underlying models \(em
.IR ballistics (2),
.IR doublependulum (2),
.IR gravity (2),
.IR atmosphere (2),
and others \(em are pure library modules with no command of their own; they are
documented separately in section 2, and are loaded by one or more of the
commands below.
.PP
Several of the classical-problem and teaching-sequence programs below
(the ones invoked as
.BI temple/ name
rather than
.BI danby/ name )
were written to accompany this same set of models but, for build reasons,
live in
.IR temple (1)'s
own directory rather than this one; they are listed here rather than there
because their documentation page names and subject matter both follow this
family.
